     wwsspp — Wellspring touchpad driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines into
     your kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee wwsspp
           ddeevviiccee hhiidd
           ddeevviiccee uussbb

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           wsp_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwsspp driver provides support for the Apple Internal Trackpad device
     found in many Apple laptops.

     The driver simulates a three-button mouse using multi-finger tap detec‐
     tion.  A single-finger press generates a left button click.  A two-finger
     tap maps to the right button; whereas a three-finger tap gets treated as
     a middle button click.

     wwsspp supports dynamic reconfiguration using sysctl(8) through nodes under
     hhww..uussbb..wwsspp.  Pointer sensitivity can be controlled using the sysctl tun‐
     able hhww..uussbb..wwsspp..ssccaallee__ffaaccttoorr.  Tap to left-click can be controlled using
     the sysctl tunable hhww..uussbb..wwsspp..eennaabbllee__ssiinnggllee__ttaapp__cclliicckkss, set to 0 to dis‐
     able single tap clicks or 1 to enable them (default).  Z-Axis sensitivity
     can be controlled using the sysctl tunable hhww..uussbb..wwsspp..zz__ffaaccttoorr.  Z-Axis
     inversion can be controlled using the sysctl tunable hhww..uussbb..wwsspp..zz__iinnvveerrtt,
     set to 0 to disable (default) or 1 to enable inversion.

FFIILLEESS
